# Previews and Overviews in Digital Libraries: Designing Surrogates to Support Visual Information Seeking.

**Authors:** Greene, Stephan, Marchionini, Gary, Plaisant, Catherine, Shneiderman, Ben

## Abstract
Presents a framework for the design of information representations in terms of previews and overviews, to aid designers of digital library interfaces. Defines previews and overviews, as graphic or textual representations of information abstracted from primary information objects, analogous to bibliographic records and catalogs; and describes four example applications. (Author/LRW)

